Identify the historical context and establishment date of the original Public Service Commission (PSC) that later evolved into the Union Public Service Commission (UPSC) in India.
The original Public Service Commission (PSC) that later evolved into the Union Public Service Commission (UPSC) in India was established on April 1, 1937, under the chairmanship of Sir Ross Barker. It was created under the Government of India Act, 1935, and initially had a limited advisory function. The Federal Public Service Commission, established under this act, became the Union Public Service Commission after India's independence.
