Determine the conservation status and historical context leading to the listing decision
The conservation status of the West Indian manatee was downgraded from "endangered" to "threatened" by the U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service (FWS) on March 30, 2017. This decision was contested by the Save the Manatee Club (SMC), which argued that the FWS failed to adequately consider data from 2010 to 2016, during which time manatees experienced unprecedented mortality events linked to habitat pollution, dependence on artificial warm water sources, and record deaths from watercraft strikes. The SMC believes the downlisting was not warranted at the time.
