Identify the original melody and lyrics of 'Twinkle Twinkle Little Star' and trace its historical origins
The original melody of "Twinkle, Twinkle, Little Star" is the French tune "Ah! vous dirai-je, maman," published in 1761. This melody was later arranged by Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart in his Twelve Variations on "Ah vous dirai-je, Maman." The lyrics are derived from an early-19th-century English poem titled "The Star" written by Jane Taylor, which was first published in 1806 in "Rhymes for the Nursery," a collection of poems by Taylor and her sister Ann Taylor. The poem was originally in couplet form and has five stanzas, although only the first is widely known and used in the song. The lyrics were first paired with the melody in "The Singing Master: First Class Tune Book" in 1838.
