**Mike Babcock:**
- **Tenure:** Mike Babcock is currently the head coach of the Toronto Maple Leafs in the NHL. He previously served as the head coach of the Detroit Red Wings for 10 seasons from 2005 to 2015.
- **Notable Achievements:** During his tenure with the Red Wings, Babcock won the Stanley Cup in 2008 and led the team to the Stanley Cup Playoffs every year. He holds the record for the most wins by a Red Wings coach, surpassing Jack Adams.
- **Background:** Born on April 29, 1963, in Canada, Babcock is a Canadian professional ice hockey head coach.

**Erik Spoelstra:**
- **Tenure:** Erik Spoelstra is the current head coach of the Miami Heat in the NBA. He was promoted to head coach in 2008 after serving as an assistant coach and director of scouting from 2001 to 2008.
- **Notable Achievements:** Spoelstra is the first Asian-American head coach in the history of the four major North American sports leagues and the first Asian-American head coach to win an NBA championship. He has led the Miami Heat to multiple NBA championships.
- **Background:** Born on November 1, 1970, in the United States, Spoelstra is of Filipino descent from his mother's side.

**Tom Thibodeau:**
- **Tenure:** Tom Thibodeau is the head coach and president of basketball operations of the Minnesota Timberwolves in the NBA. Since June 2013, he has also served as an assistant coach for the USA Basketball Men's National Team.
- **Notable Achievements:** As a defensive coach, Thibodeau helped the Houston Rockets rank among the Top 5 in the league in scoring defense and field goal percentage defense from 2004 to 2007. His teams have finished in the league's Top 10 in team defense 15 times.
- **Background:** Born on January 17, 1958, in the United States, Thibodeau is an American basketball coach.
