Identify the author of the song 'Somebody Like You' by Keith Urban, including details about the song's creation and any relevant background information.
The song "Somebody Like You" by Keith Urban was co-written by Keith Urban himself and Dave Berg. It was released in July 2002 as the first single from Urban's 2002 album "Golden Road." The song became Urban's second number one hit on the US "Billboard" Hot Country Singles & Tracks (now the Hot Country Songs) chart, spending six weeks at that position. It also peaked at number 23 on the "Billboard" Hot 100. In December 2009, "Billboard" named the song as the number one country song of the first decade of the 21st century. The music video for the song was directed by Trey Fanjoy, who also directed the video for Urban's late 2000/early 2001 single "But for the Grace of God." Urban's ex-girlfriend, Niki Taylor, appeared in the video.
