Provide details about the actor's background, notable roles, and any other significant information related to their portrayal of Christian Grey.
Jamie Dornan, born on 1 May 1982, is an actor, model, and musician from Northern Ireland. He gained recognition for his role as Sheriff Graham Humbert in the ABC series "Once Upon a Time" (2011–2013) and for portraying the serial killer Paul Spector in the BBC Two and RTÉ One crime drama series "The Fall" (2013–2016). His portrayal of Paul Spector earned him an Irish Film and Television Award for Best Actor in Television and a British Academy Television Award nomination for Best Actor.

In film, Dornan played Axel von Fersen in Sofia Coppola's "Marie Antoinette" (2006) and took on the role of Christian Grey in the "Fifty Shades" franchise (2015–2018). He was cast as Christian Grey in the film adaptation of "Fifty Shades of Grey" in October 2013, replacing Charlie Hunnam. This role marked a significant point in his career, bringing him international attention.
