Identify the different forms of dietary iron and their bioavailability
The different forms of dietary iron include heme iron and non-heme iron. Heme iron is found in animal products such as meat, poultry, and fish, and it is generally more bioavailable than non-heme iron. Non-heme iron is found in plant-based foods like beans, lentils, and fortified cereals, and its bioavailability can be influenced by other dietary factors. The bioavailability of non-heme iron is typically lower compared to heme iron.
