Identify the geographical boundaries and administrative divisions of Santa Rosa County, Florida, to determine which cities fall within its jurisdiction.
Santa Rosa County, Florida, is divided into two main regions: North Santa Rosa County and South Santa Rosa County. North Santa Rosa County includes areas from the county seat, Milton, to the northern part of the county, while South Santa Rosa County comprises the area from Holley and Navarre in the east to Gulf Breeze at the western end of the Fairpoint Peninsula, along U.S. Highway 98. A section of Santa Rosa Island, containing the unincorporated community of Navarre Beach, is also part of South Santa Rosa County. The administrative divisions include incorporated cities such as Milton, Valparaiso, and Navarre, with Navarre Beach being an unincorporated area within South Santa Rosa County. Major bodies of water like Santa Rosa Sound, Pensacola Bay, and East Bay influence the region's housing and lifestyle.
