Identify the artist and origin of the song 'Where Have All the Flowers Gone' by determining its composer, performer, and historical context
The song "Where Have All the Flowers Gone" was composed by Pete Seeger. The historical context of the song is rooted in Ukrainian and Cossack folk traditions, as the lyrics were inspired by a passage from a Ukrainian and Cossack folk song referenced in Mikhail Sholokhov's novel "And Quiet Flows the Don." Seeger adapted the lyrics to a tune based on a lumberjack version of "Drill, Ye Tarriers, Drill." The song was recorded once in a medley. The performer of the song is Pete Seeger himself.
