The standard number of games in a professional hockey season varies by league. In the National Hockey League (NHL), the regular season consists of 82 games for each team, as established since the 1995–96 season. This structure includes 41 home games and 41 road games. The American Hockey League (AHL), which serves as the primary developmental league for the NHL, typically has a regular season with 76 games per team. International tournaments, such as the Winter Olympics or the IIHF World Championships, do not follow a fixed number of games and vary depending on the tournament format and participants.
