Identify the types of waves and determine which ones require a medium for their propagation
There are two main types of waves: mechanical and electromagnetic. Mechanical waves require a medium for their propagation, while electromagnetic waves do not. Longitudinal waves and transverse waves are subtypes of mechanical waves and thus require a medium. Electromagnetic waves, such as light and radio waves, can propagate through a vacuum.
