Determine the specific models of Springfield rifles used and their distribution among Union forces
The specific models of Springfield rifles used by Union forces during the American Civil War included the Model 1855 Springfield and the Model 1861 Springfield. The Model 1855 Springfield was initially used by US Regular Army regiments, such as at the First Battle of Bull Run in July 1861. However, it was eventually replaced in the Union ranks by the Model 1861 Springfield. 

The Model 1861 Springfield became the most common weapon carried by Union infantry in the eastern theater by the middle of 1862. Western armies were slower to obtain these rifles and they were not widely used there until the middle of 1863.
