Identify the botanical structure of a carrot and determine which part contains the reproductive organs responsible for seed production
The botanical structure of a carrot is a taproot, which serves as a storage organ. The reproductive organs responsible for seed production in a carrot are located in the flower, specifically within the ovary, which is part of the female reproductive system of the plant. The ovary contains the ovules, which develop into seeds after fertilization.
