The specific literary work most commonly associated with the sword in the stone legend is "Le Morte d'Arthur" by Sir Thomas Malory. This work, published in the 15th century (around 1485), is a compilation of Arthurian legends and includes the story of the sword in the stone, which is central to the legend of King Arthur's birth and his rightful claim to the throne. The sword in the stone is a key element in the Arthurian mythos, symbolizing both destiny and divine right.
