Identify the historical figure who established the Sikh Empire and became the Maharajah of Punjab, including their reign period and key contributions to the region's governance and religious leadership.
Maharaja Ranjit Singh established the Sikh Empire and became the Maharajah of Punjab. His reign period was from 1799 to 1839. Key contributions to the region's governance included consolidating many parts of northern India into an empire, creating a secular and inclusive administration, and fostering economic growth. In terms of religious leadership, he was a devout Sikh who promoted the principles of the Khalsa, ensuring religious freedom for all faiths within his empire.
