The French and Indian War is commonly referred to as the Seven Years' War in European history. It officially began on May 18, 1754, with the Battle of Jumonville Glen, where French forces under Lieutenant Colonel Joseph Coulon de Jumonville ambushed a British expedition led by George Washington. This conflict was part of a larger global struggle between the British and French empires for colonial dominance, particularly in North America.
