Identify the final date of the last prisoner of war (POW) release from Vietnam, including the specific military branch and any relevant historical context.
The final date of the last prisoner of war (POW) release from Vietnam is June 4, 1975. This date marks the end of the Vietnam War and the release of Robert R. Garwood, who was identified as the last verified American POW from the Vietnam War. Garwood was a United States Marine Corps Private First Class. He was captured in 1965 and reportedly held by North Vietnam until his release in 1973. However, it is suggested that he may have been kept as a POW until June 4, 1975, for propaganda reasons until the war officially ended.
